cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "if you use this benchmark or its artifacts, cite it as below. the citation key of a specific .urna file is its content_hash, read with urna inspect --json."
type: dataset
title: "mtg-urna-benchmark"
version: 0.3.2
date-released: 2026-09-12
repository-code: "https://github.com/brennercruvinel/mtg-urna-benchmark"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Cruvinel
    given-names: Brenner
    affiliation: Hoff Research
    email: brenner@hoffresearch.com
abstract: "compression and retrieval benchmark of the 38,627-card magic: the gathering image corpus packed into single-file .urna containers with the urna engine: av1, avif and jpeg xl media variants, lossless batteries, inter-frame ordering over same-artwork reprints, an all-intra codec battery at matched ssimulacra2, and retrieval-only profiles measured on identity, embedding drift and text-to-image hit@k against a 3.975 GB jpeg source."
keywords:
  - image compression
  - set redundancy
  - album coding
  - av1
  - avif
  - jpeg xl
  - ssimulacra2
  - image retrieval
  - embeddings
  - vector database
  - single-file container
  - magic the gathering
  - scryfall
